{
  "_why": "Role track for PRODUCTION SUPERVISOR, a new trade (CEO Launch Plan Pack v1, Phase 2 #10, sheet 23). fam_production_supervisor binds the cross-trade NCO supervisor codes (3122.9900 Manufacturing Supervisors Other, 3122.1900 Machine Tool Operations, 3122.0601 Assembly Line Supervisor, 3122.6503 Planning Supervisor) at job-domain specificity 50; every trade-specific 3122 code stays where it is (owner ruling 2026-11-04).",
  "_scope": "SUPERVISION ACROSS TRADES OR LINES. Sheet 23's rule: a worker who picks supervisor on his own trade keeps that trade (VMC · Supervisor). This pack is for the man whose job IS the shift, the section or the line, and who does not identify with one machine trade. Bare 'supervisor' routes nowhere (A3: ask the department first).",
  "_depth": "THE TIER GATE IS supervision_experience, asked FIRST. Its options carry value_number ONLY: pack-registry.service.ts resolves valueText ?? valueNumber, and a value_text would turn every gte below into a string compare that is false forever (the #776 defect).",
  "_budget": "MAX_ENGINE_ASKS is 28 and qp_universal spends 8. Easy is 2 trade items + at most 1 confirm; Medium adds 3 (area, team size, machines); Advanced adds 3 (systems, industry, own trade). Worst case 2 + 1 + 3 + 3 = 9 trade asks.",
  "_sheet": "READ OFF CEO LAUNCH PLAN PACK v1 SHEET 23 (a new trade, no ratified page). Section title 'Supervision, team & systems'. Its rows are Areas, Team, Machines, Systems, Sector and Trade background, and every row has exactly one question here.",
